"""Central stages 34–63; textual forms and commentary remain distinct."""
from zhongshan_next30 import R

ROWS = [
R('r04-fuzhu','扶豬','Mount Fuzhu','西五十里为扶豬，多礝石。䴦貉状人目；音銀、或作麋是字音异说，不改成人面或鹿形。虢水北注洛，水中瓀石与山上礝石分卡；两段石注及䴦音注跨101—103。','Fifty li west is Mount Fuzhu, with ruan stone. Yin resembles a hao with human eyes. Guo water flows north into the Luo and contains ruan stone.','The two stone spellings and locations remain separate. Human eyes do not imply a human face; the mi variant does not supply deer anatomy.'),
R('r04-li','釐山','Mount Li','西百二十里为釐，阳玉阴蒐。犀渠牛状苍身、婴儿音；𤢺如獳犬有鳞、毛如彘鬣，郭注毛生鳞间。滽滽水南注伊，不并冝蘇同名北注河之水。108空正文续注实际在13页。','A hundred and twenty li west is Mount Li, with jade on its sunny side and sou plants on its shaded side. Xiqu is ox-shaped with a blue-green body and an infant-like cry. Yongyong water flows south into the Yi. Jie is dog-like, scaled, with pig-like bristles.','Guo Pu places the bristles between scales. The infant comparison is sound only. Unit 108 continues the commentary on scan 13, not 14; this Yongyong account remains separate from Yisu.'),
R('r04-jiwei','箕尾','Mount Jiwei','西二百里为箕尾，多榖、涂石，上有㻬琈玉。109—110玉名跨行连读，不补现代石种。','Two hundred li west is Mount Jiwei, with gu trees, tu stone and tufu jade above.','The jade name continues across units 109–110; product names do not establish modern species or mineral composition.'),
R('r04-bing','柄山','Mount Bing','西二百五十里为柄，上玉下铜；滔雕水北注洛，多羬羊。此处羬羊仅名不借他篇形貌。苃如樗、桐叶荚实，或作艾是异字，不反填成现代艾草。','Two hundred and fifty li west is Mount Bing, with jade above and copper below. Taodiao water flows north into the Luo and has qianyang. You trees resemble chu, with tong-like leaves and pods, and have an ancient fish-poisoning claim.','Qianyang is only named here. Ai is a character variant for You, not evidence that this is modern mugwort; no poisoning instructions are added.'),
R('r04-baibian','白邊','Mount Baibian','西二百里为白邊，上金玉下青雄黄；只录本段上下位置及物产，不补水名或生物。','Two hundred li west is Mount Baibian, with gold and jade above and green xionghuang below.','The above/below locations remain as written, without invented waters or creatures.'),
R('r04-xionger','熊耳','Mount Xiong-er','西二百里为熊耳，上漆下㯶。浮濠水西注洛，多水玉、人鱼；人鱼仅名，不画现代美人鱼。葶䔭如苏赤华，毒鱼为古述。117实际在14页末，植物118—119续15页。','Two hundred li west is Mount Xiong-er, with lacquer trees above and zong below. Fuhao water flows west into the Luo and contains water jade and renyu. Tingning resembles su with red flowers and has an ancient fish-poisoning claim.','Renyu has no independent anatomy here and is not depicted as a modern mermaid. Unit 117 is on scan 14; the plant account continues on 15.'),
R('r04-mu','牡山','Mount Mu','西三百里为牡，多文石、竹箭竹䉋，㸲牛羬羊仅列名，分别占位。赤鷩郭注即鷩雉，图按泛化赤雉，不强定现代物种或借翼身异兽。','Three hundred li west is Mount Mu, with patterned stones, arrow bamboo and zhumei bamboo, zuo cattle, qianyang and red Bi birds.','The cattle and qianyang are only named. The Bi image follows the commentary pheasant comparison, without a modern species identification.'),
R('r04-huanju','讙舉','Mount Huanju','西三百五十里为讙舉，雒水出而东北注玄扈，多馬腸之物，仅作未定物产存名，不按马肠字造怪兽。此二山者洛间及古地理注照录，玄扈水不擅补为本路线独立山段。','Three hundred and fifty li west is Mount Huanju. Luo water rises here and flows northeast into Xuanhu water, with much of a product called machang.','Machang is not independently classified or described. The two-mountain statement and Guo Pu geographic commentary remain textual, without an extra route mountain.'),
R('r04-summary','次四总括','Fourth-range summary and rites','釐山列鹿蹄至玄扈，九山千六百七十里。行程末名讙舉、总括末名玄扈的差异保留。神人面兽身、白鸡祈而不糈、彩饰鸡分别记录，不以祭鸡补神形。126实际在15页末。','The fourth range is stated to run from Luti to Xuanhu, with nine mountains and 1,670 li. Its gods have human faces and beast bodies. The rite uses one white chicken for prayer, without grain, and decorates it with colors.','The route ends at Huanju whereas the summary names Xuanhu; the difference is retained. The chicken rite does not provide deity anatomy. Unit 126 is on scan 15.'),
R('r05-gouchuang','茍牀','Mount Gouchuang','中次五薄山首茍牀，无草木、多怪石。郭注茍林为异名、怪石似玉，不把相似等同玉；总括称十六山而本列实际十五列名山，留差异。','The fifth Central range begins at Mount Gouchuang, with no vegetation and many unusual stones.','Guo Pu gives Goulin as a name variant and compares the stones with jade. The range later reports sixteen mountains despite fifteen named route mountains.'),
R('r05-shou','首山','Mount Shou','东三百里为首山，阴榖柞及𦬸芫，阳㻬琈玉、多槐，阴机谷有𩿁鸟。枭状三目有耳，音如錄、已墊为古述；郭注音字与未闻不补新形。','Three hundred li east is Mount Shou, with gu and zuo trees and zhu and yuan plants on its shaded side, tufu jade on its sunny side and huai trees. Ji valley has owl-like birds with three eyes and ears.','Three distinct eyes and ears are required; eye placement, ear styling, plumage and pose are artistic. The ancient eating claim and pronunciation gloss remain separate.'),
R('r05-xianzhu','縣斸','Mount Xianzhu','东三百里为縣斸，无草木、多文石，郭注音如斤斸之斸。仅保留山名与物产，不把斸字画成兵器神兽。','Three hundred li east is Mount Xianzhu, with no vegetation and abundant patterned stone.','The commentary supplies a pronunciation comparison for the name, without another entity or creature.'),
R('r05-conglong','葱聾','Mount Conglong (fifth range)','东三百里为次五葱聾，无草木、多𢈦石，郭注未详。135实际在16页末，不与首列多彩垩同名山合并。','Three hundred li east is another Mount Conglong, without vegetation and with much unidentified stone.','Guo Pu leaves the stone unknown. Unit 135 is on scan 16; this mountain remains separate from the first-range namesake.'),
R('r05-tiaogu','條谷','Mount Tiaogu','东北五百里为條谷，多槐桐，草多芍药𧄸冬。郭注满冬、今作门俗作耳为写法注，不并成三株草或宣称现代药效。','Five hundred li northeast is Mount Tiaogu, with huai and tong trees, shaoyao and mendong plants.','The commentary records name and writing variants for mendong; they are not additional plants or modern medical claims.'),
R('r05-chao','超山','Mount Chao','北十里为超，阴苍玉、阳有井，冬有水夏竭。井的季节状态照录，不反改为一般丰水期或现代气候结论。','Ten li north is Mount Chao, with cang jade on its shaded side and a well on its sunny side that has water in winter but dries in summer.','The stated seasonality remains unchanged and is not generalized into a modern hydrological rule.'),
R('r05-chenghou','成侯','Mount Chenghou','东五百里为成侯，多櫄木、芃草。似樗、车辕材、吴人称呼及音注跨140—141属于櫄，不移给芃；芃仅名。','Five hundred li east is Mount Chenghou, with chun trees and peng grass.','The chu-tree comparison, wood-use and pronunciation gloss continues across units 140–141 and belongs to Chun, not Peng.'),
R('r05-chaoge','朝歌','Mount Chaoge','东五百里为朝歌，谷多美垩。谷是谷地语境，不因美字改作美玉。','Five hundred li east is Mount Chaoge, with fine e in its valleys.','The valley context and e product term remain as written; it is not converted to jade.'),
R('r05-huai','槐山','Mount Huai','东五百里为槐山，谷多金锡。仅山名不等于本段列槐木；金锡分录，不合成现代合金。','Five hundred li east is Mount Huai, with gold and tin in its valleys.','The mountain name does not assert huai trees here, and the products do not specify an alloy.'),
R('r05-li','歴山','Mount Li (fifth range)','东十里为歴山，多槐、阳多玉，144在17页末。与歴兒及釐山分别存录，不以近似字形合并路线。','Ten li east is Mount Li, with huai trees and jade on its sunny side.','Unit 144 is on scan 17. Li-er and fourth-range Li remain separate route mountains.'),
R('r05-shi','尸山','Mount Shi','东十里为尸，多苍玉及麖。麖郭注似鹿而小黑色，据注作小黑鹿，不补角。尸水南注洛，多美玉；次五祭礼尸水合天另层关联，不将尸字画鬼尸。','Ten li east is Mount Shi, with cang jade and Jing animals. Guo Pu compares Jing with small black deer. Shi water flows south into the Luo and contains fine jade.','The small black deer form comes from commentary; antlers are not added. The later Shi-water ritual statement stays separate from the watercourse account.'),
R('r05-liangyu','良餘','Mount Liangyu','东十里为良餘，上榖柞、无石；余水出阴北注河，乳水出阳东南注洛。两水源侧、方向与受水体分别记录，不因同山合一。','Ten li east is Mount Liangyu, with gu and zuo trees above and no stone. Yu water rises on its shaded side and flows north into the He; Ru water rises on its sunny side and flows southeast into the Luo.','The two sources, directions and recipients remain distinct, without modern coordinates.'),
R('r05-guwei','蠱尾','Mount Guwei','东南十里为蠱尾，多砺石赤铜；龙余水东南注洛。龙字仅水名，不新增龙形。','Ten li southeast is Mount Guwei, with li stone and red copper. Longyu water flows southeast into the Luo.','The dragon character in the water name supplies no creature anatomy.'),
R('r05-sheng','升山','Mount Sheng','东北二十里为升，多榖柞棘、藷藇蕙冦脱。冦脱长注153—154、琁玉注154—155分别连读，不把石次玉的释义移给草。黄酸水北注河，多琁玉。','Twenty li northeast is Mount Sheng, with gu, zuo and thorn trees, shuyu, hui and koutou plants. Huangsuan water flows north into the He and has xuan jade.','Unit 153 is on scan 18. The koutou-plant gloss continues into 154; the separate xuan-stone gloss continues into 155.'),
R('r05-yangxu','陽虛','Mount Yangxu','东十二里为阳虚，多金、临玄扈水。苍颉南巡与灵龟负书丹甲青文为郭注引河图，非正文明载；灵龟图仅据注且书形为解释，不画成原文的神兽正文。','Twelve li east is Mount Yangxu, with much gold, overlooking Xuanhu water.','Guo Pu quotes a Hetu account of Cangjie and a spirit turtle bearing writing, with a red shell and blue-green markings. This is commentary, not main text; book construction and ordinary turtle anatomy in the image are artistic.'),
R('r05-summary','次五总括','Fifth-range summary and rites','薄山茍林至阳虚，十六山二千九百八十二里照录，与十五列名山留差异。升冢太牢、首山神稌黑牺蘖酿干舞、尸水天神黑犬雌鸡牝羊献血分别记录，不画祭杀。159冢仅阅读层恢复，162属19页。','The fifth range reports sixteen mountains and 2,982 li from Goulin to Yangxu. Sheng has a distinguished grand rite; Shou has rice, dark offerings, malt drink, shield dance and drum rites. The Shi-water rite mentions a black dog above, a hen below and a ewe blood offering.','The sixteen-versus-fifteen difference is retained. These are ancient ritual records, not new deity anatomy or violent illustrations. The missing zhong marker is restored only in the reading layer.'),
R('r06-pingfeng','平逢','Mount Pingfeng','中次六縞羝首平逢，南望伊洛、东望榖城，无草木，水多沙石原序照录。驕蟲人状二首，为螫虫长；蜂蜜之廬中蜜郭注赤蜂名，不读成蜂蜜液。雄鸡禳而勿杀明确保留。','The sixth Central range begins at Mount Pingfeng, looking south toward Yi-Luo and east toward Gucheng mountain. The water-and-sandstone wording is retained. Jiaochong is human-shaped with two heads and rules stinging creatures.','Guo Pu glosses mi as a red bee name. The rooster rite explicitly says not to kill it. No insect limbs or wings are added to the human-shaped two-headed god.'),
R('r06-gaodi','縞羝','Mount Gaodi','西十里为縞羝，无草木多金玉。列名与本列名分别存录，不因羝字添加公羊。','Ten li west is Mount Gaodi, without vegetation and with gold and jade.','The name supplies no ram anatomy or extra ritual offering.'),
R('r06-hui','廆山','Mount Gui (Guo Pu pronunciation)','西十里为廆，阴㻬琈玉、西有雚谷多柳楮。鴒䳩山鸡状、长尾赤如丹火、青喙；丹火为色比，不画火焰。交觴出阳南注洛，俞隨出阴北注榖。171在20页末。','Ten li west is Mount Gui, with tufu jade on its shaded side and Guan valley to its west, with willow and chu trees. Lingyao birds resemble mountain pheasants, with long red tails, cinnabar-red plumage and blue-green bills. Jiaoshang water flows south into the Luo; Yusui flows north into Gu water.','The pronunciation follows Guo Pu. Fire is a red-color comparison, not literal flames. Unit 171 is on scan 20; the waters retain their sunny/shaded sources.'),
R('r06-zhanzhu','瞻諸','Mount Zhanzhu','西三十里为瞻諸，阳金阴文石。㴬水东南注洛、少水出阴东注榖，少为水名不误读缺水；不并首列隂山少水。','Thirty li west is Mount Zhanzhu, with gold on its sunny side and patterned stone on its shaded side. Xie water flows southeast into the Luo; Shao water rises on its shaded side and flows east into Gu water.','Shao is a name here, distinct from the first-range account. The Cijian identification is commentary, not modern measured coordinates.'),
R('r06-louzhuo','婁𣵠','Mount Louzhuo','西三十里为婁𣵠，无草木多金玉。瞻水出阳东注洛、陂水出阴北注榖，多茈石文石；180在21页末，181续22页。','Thirty li west is Mount Louzhuo, with no vegetation and much gold and jade. Zhan water rises on its sunny side and flows east into the Luo; Bei water rises on its shaded side and flows north into Gu water, with zi and patterned stones.','Unit 180 is on scan 21 and 181 on 22. The Baida-water gloss is commentary; water names and mineral terms do not establish modern identities.')
]

LINKS=[]
SHARES=[]
OVERRIDES={
'water-zhongshan-he':('河（中山水文文本索引）','He (Central textual index)','甘棗、渠豬、青要、騩、冝蘇、和、良餘、升八处受水述分别保留，不认定现代水系同一性。','Eight recipient accounts at Ganzao, Quzhu, Qingyao, Wei, Yisu, He, Liangyu and Sheng remain distinct textual contexts.'),
'water-zhongshan-yi':('伊水（中山文本索引）','Yi (Central textual index)','發視、鮮、陽、葌、蔓渠及釐山六处伊水文本上下文分存，不并两处滽滽水。','Six Yi contexts remain distinct, including Li’s southward Yongyong account; this does not merge the Yisu namesake.'),
'water-zhongshan-luo':('洛（中山文本索引）','Luo (Central textual index)','各段注洛水文的方向与源侧分别存录；讙舉雒水另存，古地理注不作现代坐标。','Separate Luo recipient accounts retain their directions and source sides. The Luo source at Huanju is separately recorded.')
}

def entities(E):
    LINKS.clear();SHARES.clear();out=[];names={r['slug']:r['name'] for r in ROWS};ens={r['slug']:r['en_name'].removeprefix('Mount ') for r in ROWS}
    def add(s,k,key,n,en,q,eq,cn='',note='',**extra):
        out.append(E(s,k,key,n,en,q,cn or '本段名物与位置照录，不强定现代种属、成分或坐标。',eq,(eq+' '+note).strip(),**extra));return out[-1]['id']
    def prod(s,key,n,en,q,eq,kind='material',**extra):return add(s,kind,key,n+'（'+names[s]+'）',en+' ('+ens[s]+')',q,eq,**extra)
    def pair(a,b):LINKS.append((a,b))
    def share(id,s,q,eq):SHARES.append((id,s,q,eq))
    def water(s,key,n,en,q,eq,target=None,**extra):
        id=add(s,'water',key,n,en,q,eq,**extra)
        if target:pair(id,target);share(target,s,q,eq)
        return id
    def unknown(s,key,n,en,q,eq,kind='animal',**extra):return add(s,kind,key,n,en,q,eq,'仅有名目或类称，无本段独立形貌，不借他篇补形；统一占位不代表现代物种。','The independent form is not established here; no anatomy is borrowed from other accounts.',unknown=True,**extra)
    def form(s,key,n,en,q,eq,cn,note,kind='beast',**extra):return add(s,kind,key,n,en,q,eq,cn,note,**extra)
    def products(s,items):
        for key,n,en,q,kind in items:prod(s,key+'-'+s,n,en,q,'The account records '+en+(' on the shaded side.' if '其隂' in q else ' on the sunny side.' if '其陽' in q else ' above.' if '其上' in q else ' below.' if '其下' in q else ' in the valleys.' if '谷多' in q else ' here.'),kind=kind)
    def gj(s,q):products(s,[('gold','金','Gold',q,'material'),('jade','玉','Jade',q,'material')])
    he='water-zhongshan-he';yi='water-zhongshan-yi';luo='water-zhongshan-luo'
    s='r04-fuzhu'
    prod(s,'ruan-rock-fuzhu','礝石','Ruan stone above','其上多礝石','Ruan stone is abundant above.',commentary='音耎今鴈門山中出礝石白者；如水水中有赤色者',en_commentary='The stone gloss continues across 101–102 and mentions white and red occurrences.')
    form(s,'yin-fuzhu','䴦（扶豬）','Yin (Fuzhu)','有獸焉其狀如貉而人目其名曰䴦','Yin resembles a hao and has human eyes.','貉状人目据正文，短肢厚躯、毛色耳尾及坐姿为解释；不画成人面或借异字麋改鹿形。','Compact mammal proportions, ears, tail, fur colors and seated posture are artistic; human eyes do not imply a human face.',commentary='貉或作𧴘古字；音銀或作麋',en_commentary='Guo Pu records character variants for hao and the name, with yin pronunciation.')
    guo=water(s,'guo-fuzhu','虢水（扶豬）','Guo water (Fuzhu)','虢水出焉而北流注于洛','Guo water rises here and flows north into the Luo.',luo)
    prod(s,'ruan-water-fuzhu','瓀石','Ruan stone in water','其中多瓀石','Ruan stone is abundant in the water.',commentary='言亦出水中',en_commentary='Guo Pu says it also occurs in water.')
    s='r04-li';prod(s,'jade-li4','玉（阳）','Jade on sunny side','其陽多玉','Jade is abundant on the sunny side.')
    prod(s,'sou-li','蒐','Sou plants','其隂多蒐','Sou plants are abundant on the shaded side.',kind='plant',commentary='音捜茅蒐；今之蒨草也',en_commentary='The sou-plant gloss continues across 104–105; it is separate from Xiqu anatomy.')
    form(s,'xiqu-li','犀渠（釐山）','Xiqu (Li)','有獸焉其狀如牛蒼身其音如嬰兒是食人其名曰犀渠','Xiqu is ox-shaped with a blue-green body, sounds like an infant and is described as eating people.','牛状苍身据正文，普通牛角、四蹄、尾、色阶与低首姿为解释；婴儿仅音比，不加婴儿面，不画食人。','Ordinary ox horns, hooves, tail and posture are artistic; no infant face or violent scene is added.')
    water(s,'yongyong-li','滽滽之水（釐山）','Yongyong water (Li)','滽滽之水出焉而南流注于伊水','Yongyong water rises here and flows south into the Yi.',yi)
    form(s,'jie-li','𤢺（釐山）','Jie (Li)','有獸焉名曰𤢺其狀如獳犬而有鱗其毛如彘鬛','Jie is dog-like with scales and pig-like bristles.','如獳犬、有鳞、毛如彘鬣据文，郭注毛生鳞间；四犬足、尾、配色与回首姿为解释，不加龙角。','Ordinary dog limbs and tail, scale layout, colors and pose are artistic; bristles visibly emerge between scales.',commentary='音蒼頡之頡；生鱗間也',en_commentary='Guo Pu supplies jie pronunciation and places the bristles between scales; 108 is a commentary continuation.')
    products('r04-jiwei',[('gu','榖','Gu trees','多榖','plant'),('tu','涂石','Tu stone','多涂石','material'),('tufu','㻬琈玉','Tufu jade','其上多㻬琈之玉','material')])
    s='r04-bing';products(s,[('jade','玉','Jade','其上多玉','material'),('copper','銅','Copper','其下多銅','material')])
    tao=water(s,'taodiao-bing','滔雕之水','Taodiao water','滔雕之水出焉而北流注于洛','Taodiao water rises here and flows north into the Luo.',luo)
    q=unknown(s,'qianyang-bing','羬羊（柄山）','Qianyang (Bing)','其中多羬羊','Qianyang are abundant in the water account.');pair(tao,q)
    prod(s,'you-bing','苃','You trees','有木焉其狀如樗其葉如桐而莢實其名曰苃可以毒魚','You is a tree resembling chu, with tong-like leaves and pods, with an ancient fish-poisoning claim.',kind='plant',commentary='苃一作艾',en_commentary='Ai is a character variant, not a modern mugwort identification.')
    s='r04-baibian';gj(s,'其上多金玉');prod(s,'xionghuang-baibian','青雄黃','Green xionghuang','其下多青雄黄','Green xionghuang is abundant below.')
    s='r04-xionger';products(s,[('lacquer','漆','Lacquer trees','其上多漆','plant'),('zong','㯶','Zong trees','其下多㯶','plant')])
    fuhao=water(s,'fuhao-xionger','浮濠之水','Fuhao water','浮濠之水出焉而西流注于洛','Fuhao water rises here and flows west into the Luo.',luo)
    prod(s,'water-jade-xionger','水玉','Water jade','其中多水玉','Water jade is abundant in this water account.')
